WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.710 --> 00:00:14.809
Darmstadtium is named after the German town
of Darmstadt, which is where the big German

00:00:14.809 --> 00:00:23.250
accelerator is situated.
A letter arrived from Germany, from the institute

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:27.250
where they make all the elements from 107
up to 112. And all being well I want to go

00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:35.650
and visit the institute so that we can actually
see where these elements are being made.

00:00:35.650 --> 00:00:42.710
So we’re in Darmstadt in Germany where they
made 6 different super heavy elements and

00:00:42.710 --> 00:00:43.940
I’m just going to show you how they did
it.

00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:54.789
So imagine that this tree here is a lead target
full of atoms and here I’ve got the atom

00:00:54.789 --> 00:01:01.920
of a lighter element, say copper or iron,
and I throw it and it doesn’t stick and

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:11.939
you go on throwing and throwing, more and
more. And eventually, after days perhaps,

00:01:11.939 --> 00:01:19.640
they stick together and you make a big atom.
This is one of your new elements. And the

00:01:19.640 --> 00:01:26.409
atom flies off from the target to a detector,
and when it gets to the detector you may still

00:01:26.409 --> 00:01:33.219
be unlucky and it may all fall to bits. If
you’re really lucky little bits fall off,

00:01:33.219 --> 00:01:39.640
one particle after another. And if you do
very clever measurements from the way that

00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:46.259
these particles are formed you can work out
what the original atom was. And so you can

00:01:46.259 --> 00:01:54.180
say I’ve discovered a new element.
Well this is a door to protect the people

00:01:54.180 --> 00:02:03.210
outside from x-rays in the accelerator tunnel
here, very important for the health of the

00:02:03.210 --> 00:02:06.630
colleagues.
How heavy is the door?

00:02:06.630 --> 00:02:11.440
The door has a weight of approximately 70
tonnes because it’s filled with lead.

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:18.050
We’re finally here in the linear accelerator
hall where they accelerate the ions. So the

00:02:18.050 --> 00:02:24.240
ions start behind this wall, behind me, and
they go down quite a narrow tube. So the tube

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:31.160
is quite narrow, about 30 millimetres diameter,
and inside that there is the beam of ions.

00:02:31.160 --> 00:02:37.790
So let’s walk along and see where the ions
go.

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:45.110
By the time we get to here the ions are already
travelling at 5% of the speed of light so

00:02:45.110 --> 00:02:52.320
they accelerate enormously faster than a car
or something like that, because they’re

00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:57.820
so light. And when they get to here this is
the so-called ‘stripper’, which strips

00:02:57.820 --> 00:03:02.170
off more electrons so they can accelerate
the ions even faster. So let’s keep going

00:03:02.170 --> 00:03:08.870
and see where the experiment is.
So as we go along the here the ions are going

00:03:08.870 --> 00:03:13.660
faster and faster and faster all the time
inside the tube.

00:03:13.660 --> 00:03:22.900
So here we’re nearly at the end of the accelerator
and the experiment is over there 30 metres

00:03:22.900 --> 00:03:26.790
behind that wall. And we’ll go round and
see it in a minute.

00:03:26.790 --> 00:03:32.640
The ions here are accelerated and you can
choose the speed. If you’re driving the

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:37.000
machine flat out they can go up to 20% of
the speed of light. But that’s actually

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:42.730
too much energy for making the elements, so
for the elements you settle for only 10% of

00:03:42.730 --> 00:03:48.170
the speed of the light. And the way you make
them go fast is by putting in energy from

00:03:48.170 --> 00:03:56.100
radio waves. I’ve just been told by Ingo
here from GSI that these radio waves really

00:03:56.100 --> 00:04:02.420
are the same frequency as broadcasts and 20
years ago the American Forces Network, which

00:04:02.420 --> 00:04:08.450
used to broadcast in Germany, used to increase
their transmission power at 5 o’clock, when

00:04:08.450 --> 00:04:14.300
the soldiers went for their tea, and they
could notice this in the beam because all

00:04:14.300 --> 00:04:19.509
their control circuits suddenly responded
to the increased power of the radio station.

00:04:19.509 --> 00:04:27.069
So now we go to the region which is usually
closed during the experiment because they

00:04:27.069 --> 00:04:34.770
have radiation inside. So now this is the
place where the new elements are actually

00:04:34.770 --> 00:04:41.939
produced.
So here is the target amountage, the beam

00:04:41.939 --> 00:04:49.449
is coming from here, from the accelerator,
which you have just seen, along the tube here.

00:04:49.449 --> 00:04:55.599
Then the beam is directed into the centre
of the target and I can show you just such

00:04:55.599 --> 00:05:03.199
a target wheel which we use here. Here you
see such a target wheel which is mounted on

00:05:03.199 --> 00:05:10.439
the axis of this motor here. Then it’s like
this in the beam, the beam hits the targets

00:05:10.439 --> 00:05:18.800
here, and the wheel rotates with about 1000
revolutions per minute. Here you see the original

00:05:18.800 --> 00:05:29.060
of our target box, and all of the six elements
which were made at GSI were made here in this

00:05:29.060 --> 00:05:43.139
box.
I will show you the biggest secret now. So

00:05:43.139 --> 00:05:52.240
this is now our detector area. And here the
ions are coming from the separator and they

00:05:52.240 --> 00:06:00.110
are implanted into a silicone detector and
this detector is now within this box and now

00:06:00.110 --> 00:06:02.860
I will show you how it looks like and I will
open the box.

00:06:02.860 --> 00:06:10.080
I’m very excited, never seen anything like
this before, so it’s really a real first

00:06:10.080 --> 00:06:15.849
for me, I’ve never met anybody who’s discovered
an element.

00:06:15.849 --> 00:06:25.389
So now you see our secret. You see this is
the main part for the identification and detection

00:06:25.389 --> 00:06:30.969
of the elements. The beam comes from here
and this detector is then mounted in this

00:06:30.969 --> 00:06:38.550
direction here. The whole system is cooled
to minus 20 degrees, and this gives us a much

00:06:38.550 --> 00:06:44.180
better energy resolution. When a particle
comes into the detector we measure the time

00:06:44.180 --> 00:06:51.999
when it arrived and this can be done within
a microsecond you will see. Then we measure

00:06:51.999 --> 00:06:59.080
the energy of the particle which comes into
the detector and we measure at which place

00:06:59.080 --> 00:07:04.879
in the detector, and this we can do with the
position of point one millimetre. Usually

00:07:04.879 --> 00:07:11.620
this is hidden in the vacuum box and you don’t
see it I just opened it to show it to you.

00:07:11.620 --> 00:07:17.689
Do you feel like this is a piece of history?
Certainly. Our first version which we had

00:07:17.689 --> 00:07:26.419
is already in the museum in the Deutsches
Museum in Bonn now. This is already a second

00:07:26.419 --> 00:07:31.770
version and an improved one.
Yes with the detector in the museum we saw

00:07:31.770 --> 00:07:39.029
all the elements under 700, 800, 9. With this
detector we saw under 10, 11 and 12.

